# Ignore everything without an extension, then selectively allow files and directories.
*
!*.*
!*/

# Don't ignore makefiles and license files.
!makefile
!Makefile
!LICENSE
!LICENSE-CODE

# Ignore the simulator harness binary, built by `make -C ci/simcheck`.
ci/simcheck/simcheck

# Ignore assembler output, wherever an assembler run by hand leaves it.
*.hex
*.obj
*.lst
*.lss
*.map
*.eep

# Ignore Microchip Studio projects and their build output. The course ships .asm files; a Studio
# project is something each participant creates around one.
*.atsln
*.asmproj
*.componentinfo.xml
Debug/
Release/
.vs/

# Ignore the Python environment and bytecode used to redraw the diagrams.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Ignore IDE directories.
.vscode/
.claude/

# Ignore temp/ directory.
temp/

# Solutions are published after each lecture, not with it. They sit in the working tree so the
# course can be checked end to end (ci/simtest.py assembles and simulates the lab solutions), and
# are force-added once the lecture has been given:
#   git add -f lectures/L01/appendix/d_solutions.md
*_solutions.md
labs/lab3/solutions/

# Figures used only by a solutions appendix are named sol_*.png, and follow their appendix: they
# are force-added together with it. Otherwise the check that every committed figure is embedded
# somewhere would fail on a figure whose only reader has not been published yet.
lectures/*/appendix/images/sol_*.png

# The written exam and its solutions are the teacher's alone and are never published; the
# solutions are handed out on paper when the marked exam is returned. The practice exam and its
# solutions are published from the start, since students train on them before L12.
!exam/practice_exam_solutions.md
exam/exam.md
exam/images/exam_*.png
